  "releaseNotes": "BREAKING: RSA key material now crosses the public surface as a reusable RsaKey handle instead of PEM text. Every PEM-string overload on IPublicKeyService was removed outright — nothing was deprecated, so there is no transition window — GenerateRsaKeyPair became GenerateRsaKey, and the per-call char[] password parameter is gone: a passphrase is supplied once, at RsaKey.ImportPrivateKeyPem. IX509CertificateService moved to the same handle, and ImportPkcs12 now returns (string certificatePem, RsaKey privateKey). Encrypted private keys are now written as PBES2 (PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256, AES-256-CBC); reading still accepts unencrypted PKCS#8, PBES2 and traditional-OpenSSL, so existing key files keep working — only the API breaks, not the files. New: ML-DSA and ML-KEM key PEM services, and a Checksum module with seven CRC-16/CRC-32 variants (error detection, never a security primitive). Still targets netstandard2.0/net8.0/net10.0 on BouncyCastle 2.7.0. See RELEASENOTES.md for the full details.",
